{#- A pair's first direction question, as `decide()` asks it
    (`reconcile.build_items`, a choice under the id `from` over the record
    letters, null allowed; asked only under `reconcile.PAIR_VOCABULARIES`).
    No vars. The retired one-call prompt's direction sentence: its rules
    word for word, its opening reworded because an empty string is not an
    option and null is. -#}
For "duplicate", "continuation", "subthread" and "pays_off", give the direction as letters in "from" and "to", and null for both when the decision has no direction: for "duplicate", "from" is the record to fold away and "to" the one to keep; "from" continues "to", or is a subthread of "to"; for "pays_off", "from" is the plot thread and "to" the commitment.
